  "progression": {
    "method": "double-progression",
    "instructions": "Choose a load that allows the lower end of the rep range with controlled technique and a few repetitions left. Add repetitions before weight. When every working set reaches the upper end on two exposures, try the smallest available load increase and return to the lower end. For bodyweight or timed holds, add repetitions or seconds within the range before choosing a harder variation.",
    "stall": "If performance drops for two exposures, keep the load and review technique, sleep and training volume. If still struggling, reduce load by about 5\u201310% or remove one accessory set for a week, then reassess. This is manual guidance, not an automatic load change."
  },
